! ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!  osmo-hnbgw — the gateway a DPH femtocell speaks Iuh to.
!
!  TEMPLATE. Replace every <PLACEHOLDER>. Deploy with something like:
!    sudo install -o osmocom -g osmocom -m 660 osmo-hnbgw.cfg /etc/osmocom/
!
!  ⛔ DO NOT paste this over a working config without reading it first. A restore
!     procedure and an overwrite look identical from inside the command.
! ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!
!  Role: the femtocell speaks Iuh (SCTP/29169) to this daemon; this daemon
!  speaks RANAP onward to osmo-stp -> osmo-msc.
!
!  ⭐ osmo-hnbgw is vendor-neutral. Source-read, not assumed: the HNB register
!     handler copies the HNB identity string verbatim without validating it, and
!     the accept-all policy takes any conformant hNodeB. It rejects only on ASN.1
!     decode failure, a getpeername() failure, an unknown HNB under a closed
!     policy, or a duplicate cell identity. THE GATEWAY WILL TAKE A MICROCELL.
!     Whatever is failing during bring-up, it is almost certainly device-side.
!
log stderr
 logging color 1
 logging print category 1
 logging print level 1
 logging print file basename last
 logging level set-all notice
 !
 ! ⭐ TURN THESE UP FOR BRING-UP. They render the HNBAP register exchange at IE
 !    level, which is the only way to see WHY a register was refused.
 ! ⚠️ SUCCESS AND FAILURE MAY NOT LOG AT THE SAME SEVERITY. On a sibling stack
 !    the successful path logged at DEBUG and the failure path at ERROR -- so
 !    with DEBUG off, a count of outcomes is 100% failures BY CONSTRUCTION and
 !    the query producing it is perfectly correct. Check that both paths log at
 !    the same level before you count outcomes in a log.
 logging level hnbap debug
 logging level rua debug
 logging level ranap debug
!
line vty
 no login
!
hnbgw
 !
 ! ── PLMN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 ! ⛔ NEVER a real carrier's MCC/MNC. 999-99 is ITU-reserved for private use;
 !    001-01 is the 3GPP test network. Must match osmo-msc and your SIMs.
 plmn 999 99
 !
 ! ── The RAB assignment timer ────────────────────────────────────────────────
 ! 🔴 THE DEFAULT IS TOO SHORT FOR THIS HARDWARE.
 !    Default X1002 is 10 s. Our AP answers RAB Assignment at 12-13 s, so at the
 !    default the gateway tears the call down BEFORE the response arrives -- and
 !    almost no capture ever contains a RAB-AssignmentResponse, which sends you
 !    hunting a missing message that was merely late.
 timer mgw X1002 30
 !
 iuh
  ! ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ! 🔴 SET A SPECIFIC ADDRESS. DO NOT USE 0.0.0.0.
  !
  ! With a wildcard bind, osmo-hnbgw advertises EVERY local address in the SCTP
  ! INIT-ACK -- including transient ones such as GGSN subscriber tunnels. We
  ! measured FOUR paths offered to the AP, two of which the AP could not route
  ! to. With a 5 s heartbeat and a 2-retransmission path limit, the dead paths
  ! accumulate failures and THE ASSOCIATION ABORTS at ~25 s, over and over.
  !
  ! ⭐ AND WHY IT "WORKED BEFORE": SCTP fixes its address list AT ASSOCIATION
  !    SETUP. The previous association was established before those tunnels
  !    existed, so only the real addresses were ever advertised. SAME CONFIG,
  !    DIFFERENT STARTUP ORDER. Diffing the config against a known-good state
  !    finds nothing, because the config is correct in both states.
  !
  ! ⇒ Any daemon left on a wildcard bind re-acquires this the moment a new
  !   interface appears. The right question is not "what changed in the config"
  !   but "what exists right now that did not before".
  ! ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  local-ip <THIS-HOST-LAN-IP>
 !
 ! ── Media gateway ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 ! A dedicated MGW instance for the 3G IuUP/RTP path is cleaner than sharing the
 ! MSC's. Use a distinct port so the two do not collide.
 ! ⚠️ Two instances of one binary DO NOT have one role. Settings that are correct
 !    on the core-facing MGW can be wrong on the AP-facing one. Symmetry between
 !    them is a hypothesis, not a licence.
 mgw 0
  remote-ip 127.0.0.1
  local-port 2729
  remote-port <MGW-PORT>
  reset-endpoint rtpbridge/*
